WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.703
-After slogging through
months of painful

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.672
negotiations over
their domestic agenda,

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.407
Democratic leaders
and President Biden

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.776
claimed today that
they´ve reached a deal

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.444
on a framework
for a massive bill

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:14.314
to expand the social safety net,
but it´s still not clear

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.749
if there are enough votes
for the plan.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.385
For more on this,
it´s time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:22.455
♫♫

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.224
To give you an idea of
how things are going

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.392
in Congress right now,

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.627
here´s a photo
Utah Senator Mitt Romney

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.997
posted today of himself
dressed up as Ted Lasso,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.198
serving biscuits to

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:35.001
Democratic Senator
Kyrsten Sinema.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.436
Man, you know you´re unpopular
when you can

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:40.340
single-handedly ruin one of
America´s favorite TV shows.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.541
This is like when Rudy Giuliani

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:42.776
ran out of
the White House bathroom

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:43.910
with his pants
around his ankles,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.312
George Costanza-style.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.415
Or like when Nixon showed up
to a press conference

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.749
dressed as Radar O´Reilly.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:53.119
The "M.A.S.H."
references are back!

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.522
But this just proves once again
that we desperately need

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.757
Roy Kent in Congress,
because that picture

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.892
makes me want to...

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.893
-[Bleep]

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.694
-Now,

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.430
even if you only been
paying cursory attention

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.898
to the news lately,
you´ve probably heard

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.366
that Democratic negotiations

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.767
over their
massive infrastructure

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.903
and social safety net bills
have been --

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:12.572
and this is the exact
political science term,

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.841
originally coined by historian
Doris Kearns Goodwin

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.176
in her prize-winning study

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.311
of power and influence
in the 19th century --

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.946
a [bleep]-covered,
ass-over-teakettle

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.082
cluster[bleep].

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.250
That´s from the X-rated version
of her famous book,

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.619
"Team of Mother[bleep] Rivals."

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.354
By the way, that is
the most high-minded joke

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:31.624
you´ll hear tonight that also
has three bleeps in it.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.193
The process has been
a brutal slog,

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:35.528
thanks almost entirely
to two centrist Democrats,

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.763
Joe Manchin
and Kyrsten Sinema,

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.264
who decided to
hold the bill hostage

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.699
and turn it into
a public melodrama

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:42.502
to feed their own egos and to
protect their corporate patrons.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.704
Sinema´s raked in money from
Wall Street and Big Pharma,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.606
and Manchin has been
called a kingmaker

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.074
by fossil fuel lobbyists

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.443
and personally profits from
the coal industry in his state.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.644
And yet Manchin frequently

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.047
does a "woe is me" routine
for reporters,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.583
like earlier this week
when he seemed to agree

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:59.486
that life might be easier
for him if he were a Republican.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.122
-Have you ever thought life
would be easier for you

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:05.525
if you shifted
to being a Republican?

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.361
And somebody had said recently
that, you know,

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.063
people have approached
you about doing that.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.965
-Every day.
-Every day?

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.834
-Well, either that or just --

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.936
-It might be easier
for you to do that?

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.439
-Oh, I´d be much easier.
My goodness´ sake.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.574
But is that the purpose of being
involved in public service?

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.575
Because it´s easy?

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.877
-Are you thinking
about doing it?

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.312
-No, I´ve never. I´ve
never thought from this....

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.915
What I´m telling you now
is who I am.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.050
Do you think by having
a D or an I or an R,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.752
it´s going to change who I am?

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.487
I don´t think the R´s would
be any more happier with me

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.855
than the D´s are right now.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.457
Okay?

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.859
I mean, that´s about
as blunt as I can put it,

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.295
so I don´t know
where in the hell I belong.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:46.666
-Man, this adaptation
of "Dear Evan Hansen" sucks.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.368
They should never have
left someone that old

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.369
play a high schooler.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:52.372
But seriously,
is this a musical?

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.973
Are you about
to break out into song?

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.075
He looks like you should be
sitting next to a fake window,

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.211
looking at a cardboard
cut-out of the moon.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.480
♫ I have D next to my name ♫

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.448
♫ But I´m not sure that
I´m the same ♫

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.817
♫ Where do I belong? ♫

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:08.588
[ Scattered applause ]

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:12.058
I think there was seriously
one, solitary clap,

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.560
but it was like
a reverse clap.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.328
It was this.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.166
This is all just
a self-aggrandizing shtick

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.001
from two senators
who want to be seen

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.337
as straight-,hooting
middle-of-the-road dealmakers,

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.106
but who are in reality
just protecting their interests

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.841
of the corporate patrons
and themselves.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.643
I mean,
Manchin literally has a stake

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.045
in a family-owned coal company

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.414
in his so-called houseboat
named Almost Heaven,

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.282
where he was confronted
recently by activists

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:39.852
who literally kayaked there
to ask him questions.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.354
-I´m sorry,
but that´s not a houseboat.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:43.223
That´s a yacht.
You know how I know?

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:46.292
Houseboats don´t have
cursive on them.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.428
A houseboat´s something
a grizzled, retired cop

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:50.363
played by Clint Eastwood
or Tommy Lee Jones

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.165
lives on in a movie
where a young rookie

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:54.634
comes to him asking for help
catching the Alphabet Killer.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.603
"I told you, I´m not
on the force anymore."

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:58.504
"But you´re the only one who´s
come close to catching him."

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.441
"Didn´t you hear me, damn it?
I´m not a cop anymore.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:04.911
Hell, I´m not even a man
after Janice left me.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.346
I don´t know
where the hell I belong."

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:08.581
♫ Oh, where do I belong? ♫

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.719
[ Applause ]

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:19.659
Manchin has been the key foe of
budget chairman Bernie Sanders,

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.828
who´s been pushing
for the full package

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.463
that originally included,
among other things,

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:26.032
drug pricing reform,
tuition-free community college,

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.333
paid family and medical leave,

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:30.103
Medicare benefits for
hearing, vision, and dental,

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.638
and significant
climate provisions

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:34.107
to help stave off,
you know, planetary collapse.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.708
Although, I guess
you´re not too worried

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:39.078
about rising sea levels
when your house is also a boat.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.546
Publicly,
in front of the cameras,

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.548
Manchin has very much tried
to make it look like

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.517
he´s negotiating
in good faith with Bernie,

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:47.220
like when he wandered over
to pose for pictures with Bernie

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.521
in the Capitol parking lot
before

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:49.789
they each got into their cars.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.658
-Here, get a picture.
You want to get a picture?

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:54.861
-Get a picture of us, huh?

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:56.596
-We´re talking.
-We´re talking.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.730
-You´re going to have
a resolution

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.731
by the end of the week
at some point?

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.066
-We´re talking.
-We´re talking.

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:01.501
We´re going
to make some progress.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.903
-Senator Sanders, are you
prepared to make some deep cuts

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:06.072
to climate change
and other things like that?

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.106
-Guys, watch the vehicles,
please.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.107
Come on out.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.542
That vehicle´s going
to come out.

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.411
-My favorite part of
that clip is at the end,

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.880
when Manchin slides
comfortably into a giant pickup

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.316
and Bernie squeezes into
what I can only assume

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.284
is the smallest
compact car on the market

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.586
that came pre-installed
with three carpoolers.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.488
-[ As Bernie Sanders ]
"No radio, no chitchat,

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:25.725
just off to work
and home again."

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:28.094
And it is very on-brand
that Bernie

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:30.163
is much less enthusiastic
than Manchin

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.331
for a bull[bleep] photo op.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.700
Manchin´s got the energy
of a used car salesman

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.835
shooting his own commercial,
and Bernie is having none of it.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.236
"Yep, sure. We´re talking.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.805
And as you know, famously,

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.973
talking is
my favorite thing to do.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.709
I just love to sit around
and waste time

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:45.278
making small talk with guys
who live on houseboats.

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:46.746
Why don´t we exchange
phone numbers

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:47.814
so you can call me

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:48.981
and we can stay up
until 3:00 AM,

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.751
talking about
our hopes and dreams,

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:54.354
what we´re going
to wear to prom?

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:55.788
And then maybe after
that we can find some time

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.757
to make some matching
friendship places."

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:04.630
But in private, Manchin has
been much more hostile

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.798
to Bernie´s agenda --

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:07.433
an agenda President Biden
himself, mind you,

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.735
has said he was fully behind.

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:11.003
"Axios" reported last week
that Manchin threatened

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.505
in a meeting with Bernie
and other Democrats

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:14.707
to kill both the bigger
social safety net bill

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:17.176
and a bipartisan
infrastructure bill.

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.078
Manchin and Sanders
squabbled behind closed doors,

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:21.514
with Manchin using
a raised-fist "goose egg"

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:23.316
to tell his colleague
he can live without

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:25.718
any of the president´s
social spending plan.

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.120
According to one senator
in the room,

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.421
Joe said, "I´m comfortable
with nothing."

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.923
Bernie said, "We need
to do $3.5 trillion."

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.792
Manchin said,
"I´m comfortable with zero,"

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:35.194
forming a zero with
his thumb and index finger.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.362
Alright, first of all,
never get into

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:37.930
a hand gesture battle
with Bernie Sanders.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.932
The man uses his index fingers

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.435
the way ninjas use
throwing stars.

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:44.003
Remember the debate?
He never had to say a word.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.405
He´d just raise
that index finger

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:46.672
while someone else was talking,
and it would be like

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:49.809
watching The Rock
pick up his microphone.

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:51.310
But say all you want
about Manchin --

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.879
and clearly, we´ve said a lot.

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:54.947
At least he´s a Democrat
from West Virginia,

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.616
where Trump won
by almost 40 points.

00:06:56.616 --> 00:06:58.251
Sinema, on the other hand,
is from Arizona --

00:06:58.251 --> 00:07:00.253
a state Joe Biden won --
where her poll numbers

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:02.188
among Democrats
have collapsed

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:03.589
thanks to her obstructionism.

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:05.425
And unlike Manchin, she never
even talks to the press --

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:06.859
or to voters, for that matter.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:08.795
She holds private fundraisers
and meetings with lobbyists.

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:10.329
But then, when constituents
and reporters try

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:12.064
to get answers out of her,
this happens.

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:34.821
[ Radio chatter ]

00:07:38.558 --> 00:07:39.859
Man, reporters
are getting desperate.

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:41.127
They´re starting to sound
like a family

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.328
trapped in an escape room.

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:44.263
Puzzle-master!
Can you give us a clue?

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:47.166
Anything?!
We´ve been here for three days!

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:48.868
Sinema blocked everything
from increased taxes

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.436
on the wealthy
to drug pricing reform --

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:52.104
some of the most popular
components of the bill.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:53.706
And in the process,
she and Manchin have turned

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:56.375
an entire negotiation
into a nightmare slog

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.511
to the point where even
reporters and correspondents

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:00.046
are having trouble keeping up

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:01.447
with what´s in the bill
and what´s not.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:04.684
Likely in -- universal pre-K,

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:07.620
a one-year extension
of the Child Tax Credit,

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:11.290
childcare center funding,
Pell Grant increases,

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:14.193
some unspecified
climate change funding,

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:16.662
and an elder care provision.

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:19.232
Now, here´s what might be out.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:20.466
Free community college.

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:22.435
This was very important
to progressives.

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.203
Expanded Medicare coverage.

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:27.773
That includes dental, vision,
and hearing coverage.

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:30.042
The Clean Electricity
Performance Program.

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:32.411
That is a major
climate initiative.

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:34.514
And tax hikes on corporations

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:36.415
and high earners.

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:37.717
What´s still under discussion?

00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:42.054
Well, an $800 Medicare
dental voucher program,

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:45.625
four weeks of federal
paid family leave,

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.059
expansions in red states

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:48.794
that haven´t
expanded it already,

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:52.398
and, to pay for it --
you´ve heard a lot about this --

00:08:52.398 --> 00:08:54.133
a billionaire wealth tax.

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:56.068
So, it´s a lot to cover.

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:57.303
Out -- mom jeans.

00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:58.738
In -- hip-huggers.

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:00.072
Out -- the Kardashians.

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:02.708
In -- the Jenners.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.143
This process has been so chaotic

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:05.478
they had to break out
the big board.

00:09:05.478 --> 00:09:06.779
Next thing you know,
they´re gonna run

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:08.915
Steve Kornacki out there
to do math on the fly

00:09:08.915 --> 00:09:10.516
while they feed him
a steady diet

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.652
of paper and Sharpie.

00:09:12.652 --> 00:09:14.420
Now, the list of what´s in
includes a lot

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.889
of great transformative stuff
like the child tax credit,

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:18.658
universal pre-K,
and some major climate stuff,

00:09:18.658 --> 00:09:20.960
among other things, but the list
of what´s out is infuriating.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:23.729
For one thing, how can anyone be
against drug pricing reform

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:25.831
or free community college
or paid family leave?

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.667
We´re one of only
a small handful of countries

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:28.901
that doesn´t have it --
it´s insane.

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:31.137
Everyone deserves the right
to be at home

00:09:31.137 --> 00:09:32.338
with their families
and children.

00:09:32.338 --> 00:09:34.206
And besides --
in my experience,

00:09:34.206 --> 00:09:35.808
the more time you spend
with your kids,

00:09:35.808 --> 00:09:38.844
the more desperate you are
to go back to work.

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:40.479
After a week of lockdown
with my family,

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:41.714
I called up NBC and said,

00:09:41.714 --> 00:09:45.017
"We need to do the show
in the attic!"

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:46.619
By the way, I still
can´t believe we lost

00:09:46.619 --> 00:09:49.488
the Best Show In An Attic Emmy
to BBC´s period drama,

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:52.191
"Upstairs: Even More Upstairs."

00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:54.827
And that´s a perfect example
of the kind of high-effort,

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:57.563
low-return joke
we learned to tell...

00:09:57.563 --> 00:10:00.299
when doing a show in an attic.

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:04.003
That joke would have killed
in the attic.

00:10:04.003 --> 00:10:05.738
The audience
would have been buzzing

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:08.240
because the audience were wasps.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.575
[ Laughter ]

00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:14.413
But after all the obstructionism
and hostage-taking

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:16.449
and painful cuts today,
Democrats claim they had

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:18.484
a tentative deal
on a framework for a bill,

00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:20.653
and Biden himself
went to the Hill to tout it,

00:10:20.653 --> 00:10:22.455
claiming everyone was on board.

00:10:32.331 --> 00:10:34.166
-Is Bernie Sanders
on board, sir?

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.705
-It´s not a good sign
when Biden´s talking

00:10:39.705 --> 00:10:42.808
like an Amtrak conductor
who dozed off.

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:44.910
"Hey, man, shouldn´t you be
saying ´all aboard´?"

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.712
"Why? I´m on board.
You´re on board.

00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:48.147
We´re all on board, right?"

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:52.084
So, there you go --
the process was painful,

00:10:52.084 --> 00:10:53.352
the cuts were brutal,

00:10:53.352 --> 00:10:55.755
but at least now, finally,
Democrats have a deal

00:10:55.755 --> 00:10:57.356
everyone can get behind, right?

00:10:57.356 --> 00:10:59.191
-And We heard from
Senator Dick Durbin

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:00.926
a short time ago
after the meeting started.

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:02.428
He said, "I wish
I could say yes,

00:11:02.428 --> 00:11:05.531
but there´s a great deal of
uncertainty within the caucus."

00:11:05.531 --> 00:11:06.832
He was asked
if he´s confident

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:08.968
all 50 Democrats in the Senate
are on board.

00:11:08.968 --> 00:11:10.736
He couldn´t say yes.

00:11:10.736 --> 00:11:13.506
-What? Then, what the hell was
this announcement all about?

00:11:13.506 --> 00:11:16.409
Don´t tout the deal
unless the deal is done.

00:11:16.409 --> 00:11:18.911
Don´t be the dad that says,
"Who wants to go to Disneyland?"

00:11:18.911 --> 00:11:20.780
And then, after
the kids scream "yes"

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.015
go online to see
if tickets are available.

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:25.718
Okay. Just remember, kids --
we have very inflexible dates,

00:11:25.718 --> 00:11:27.386
so fingers crossed."

00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:30.256
Ohhhh, shoot, shoot, shoot,
shoot, shoot, shoot, shoot.

00:11:30.256 --> 00:11:32.058
Who wants to go
to Busch Gardens?

00:11:32.058 --> 00:11:34.260
Stop hitting me!

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.595
I am your father!

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:39.298
Don´t you throw
that "Lego brick" at me.

00:11:39.298 --> 00:11:41.167
[ Laughter ]

00:11:42.535 --> 00:11:44.470
The stakes for this bill
cannot be overstated.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.739
Democrats have to deliver
on their promises,

00:11:46.739 --> 00:11:48.507
boost the economy,
and give voters a reason

00:11:48.507 --> 00:11:49.842
to keep them in office.

00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:51.644
Otherwise, the people
who could very well take power

00:11:51.644 --> 00:11:54.580
in 2022 and 2024
are the GOP cult

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:57.049
of authoritarian weirdos,
leaving the rest of us to say,

00:11:57.049 --> 00:11:59.552
"I don´t know
where in the hell I belong."

00:11:59.552 --> 00:12:01.687
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:01.687 --> 00:12:05.124
